# Light SDK tool rules

You are working in the official [light-sdk](https://github.com/lightphone/light-sdk) scaffold. Custom apps are **tools** built inside `:tool`, not blank Android apps.

## Where to edit

- Write app code in `tool/` (and study `examples/` for patterns).
- Put id/label/version/permissions in `tool/lighttool.toml` — never set `applicationId`, `versionCode`, `versionName`, or `namespace` in Gradle.
- Do not casually change `:plugin` allowlists or lint rules if the tool should stay Light-signable later.

## Architecture

- Kotlin + Compose + Coroutines + MVVM.
- Screens extend `LightScreen` / `SimpleLightScreen`; VMs extend `LightViewModel`.
- Exactly one `@InitialScreen`. Navigate with `navigateTo(::OtherScreen)`; return with `goBack(result)`.
- Prefer `com.thelightphone.sdk.ui.*` (`LightText`, `LightIcon`, `LightTheme`, `lightClickable`, …).
- Background work: `@LightJob` + `LightWork`. Optional `@EntryPoint` for app-wide setup/push.

## Hard blocks (build will fail)

Do **not** use: Activities/Intents, `LocalContext` / `LocalView` / `LocalLifecycleOwner`, `startActivity`, `getSystemService`, `contentResolver`, reflection, custom `BroadcastReceiver`/`Service` wiring.

Allowed deps include Compose, Coroutines, OkHttp, Ktor, Room, WorkManager, DataStore, UnifiedPush, kotlinx-serialization. Anything else needs an allowlist change upstream.

Allowed permissions (in `lighttool.toml` only): INTERNET, ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE, WAKE_LOCK, VIBRATE, POST_NOTIFICATIONS, CAMERA, RECORD_AUDIO, READ_MEDIA_AUDIO, ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION, ACCESS_COARSE_LOCATION, NFC.

## Patterns

```kotlin
@InitialScreen
class HomeScreen(activity: SealedLightActivity) : LightScreen<Unit, HomeScreenViewModel>(activity) {
    override val viewModelClass = HomeScreenViewModel::class.java
    override fun createViewModel() = HomeScreenViewModel()
    @Composable override fun Content() { /* LightTheme + LightText */ }
}
```

Copy structure from `examples/ui-demo`, `examples/weather`, or `examples/authenticator`.

## Upstream PRs

Light expects human-owned issues/PRs; keep comments brief and in your voice. See `CONTRIBUTING.md`.
